D("outwit",{etymology:E("Formed from out- ‘surpass’ + wit, from Old English wit ‘understanding’; it means gain an advantage through quicker or cleverer thinking.","out-","wit",null,"Etymonline, outwit (https://www.etymonline.com/word/outwit)."),contexts:[C("outwit.s1","通用","The detective outwitted the thief by predicting the hidden route and waiting at the exit.","偵探預測了隱藏路線並在出口等候，靠機智勝過了竊賊。","Outwit means defeat or gain an advantage over someone by clever thinking.","Transitive past verb with thief as object; by gives the method.","The detective anticipates the thief’s plan and gains the advantage.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The detective outwitted the thief by following the thief’s plan exactly and falling into the trap.","The detective was outwitted by the thief after following the plan into the trap.","Outwit means be cleverer and gain an advantage; falling into the opponent’s trap means the detective was outwitted.")],quiz:[Q("outwit.q1","outwit.s1","meaning","To outwit a rival is to ___.",["gain an advantage through cleverness","give the rival a gift","copy the rival’s clothes"],"gain an advantage through cleverness","Outwit means defeat someone by thinking faster or more cleverly.","meaning"),Q("outwit.q2","outwit.s1","context","Which character outwits the guard?",["A prisoner distracts the guard with a clever decoy and escapes.","A prisoner follows every guard instruction and stays put.","A guard accidentally drops a key."],"A prisoner distracts the guard with a clever decoy and escapes.","The prisoner uses a clever plan to gain an advantage.","context"),Q("outwit.q3","outwit.s1","verb-form","Choose the past tense: “The fox ____ the hounds.”",["outwitted","outwit","outwitting"],"outwitted","The regular past form adds -ed to outwit, doubling t in spelling.","verb-form"),Q("outwit.q4","outwit.s1","word-choice","She used a clever riddle to ____ the puzzle champion.",["outwit","outwash","outstretch"],"outwit","The context calls for defeating someone through cleverness.","word-choice")]});
D("outwork",{etymology:E("A compound of out + work; it can mean work harder or more effectively than someone, and as a noun it can refer to work done away from a central workplace or an outer fortification.",null,"out + work",null,"Merriam-Webster, outwork (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/outwork)."),contexts:[C("outwork.s1","工作","The runner outworked his competitors by training consistently through the winter.","這位跑者整個冬天持續訓練，付出比對手更多的努力。","As a verb, outwork means work harder or more effectively than someone.","Past-tense verb with competitors as object; by introduces how he did it.","Consistent winter training gives him a greater work effort than rivals."),C("outwork.s2","军事","The old fort’s outwork protected the main gate from a direct attack.","古堡的外堡保護主門免受正面攻擊。","As a noun, an outwork is an outer defensive structure beyond the main fort.","Possessive fort’s modifies the count noun; from marks the threat.","The structure lies outside and protects the fort’s central defenses.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The fort’s outwork stood inside the keep and formed the innermost room of the castle.","The fort’s outwork stood beyond the main defenses and helped protect the approach.","An outwork is an outer fortification, not an interior room of the central keep.")],quiz:[Q("outwork.q1","outwork.s1","meaning","A team that outworks its rival ___.",["works harder or more effectively","works fewer hours by rule","leaves before the task begins"],"works harder or more effectively","The verb means surpass someone in amount or effectiveness of work.","meaning"),Q("outwork.q2","outwork.s2","meaning","A fort’s outwork is ___.",["an outer defensive structure","the central dining hall","a worker’s time sheet"],"an outer defensive structure","The noun sense is a defensive work built outside the main fort.","meaning"),Q("outwork.q3","outwork.s1","context","Which sentence uses outwork as a verb?",["She outworked the other candidates during the training season.","The stone outwork guarded the gate.","The outer wall was repaired."],"She outworked the other candidates during the training season.","Outworked is an action comparing her work effort with theirs.","context"),Q("outwork.q4","outwork.s2","context","Where would an archaeologist find an outwork?",["Beyond a fort’s main wall as part of its defenses","At the center of a modern office desk","Inside a cooking oven"],"Beyond a fort’s main wall as part of its defenses","The structure is an outer defense outside the central fort.","context")]});
D("oval",{etymology:E("From Latin ovalis ‘egg-shaped’, from ovum ‘egg’; English uses oval as both an adjective and a noun for a rounded shape longer than it is wide.",null,"Latin ovalis < ovum",null,"Etymonline, oval (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oval)."),contexts:[C("oval.s1","形状","The mirror has an oval frame that is longer vertically than it is wide.","這面鏡子有一個縱向較長的橢圓形框。","Oval as an adjective describes a rounded, egg-like shape longer than it is wide.","Attributive adjective before frame; that clause specifies its proportions.","The frame is elongated and rounded, like an egg."),C("oval.s2","形状","She drew an oval around the correct answer on the worksheet.","她在練習單的正確答案周圍畫了一個橢圓。","Oval as a noun names a figure or object with that rounded shape.","An oval is the direct object of drew; around identifies what it encloses.","The drawn figure itself has the oval shape.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The plate was oval, with four sharp corners and every side the same length.","The plate was rectangular, with four sharp corners and every side the same length.","An oval is rounded and has no sharp corners; the described shape is rectangular.")],quiz:[Q("oval.q1","oval.s1","meaning","An oval mirror is generally ___.",["rounded and longer in one direction","a perfect circle with no longer axis","a sharp-edged triangle"],"rounded and longer in one direction","Oval describes an egg-like rounded shape longer than it is wide.","meaning"),Q("oval.q2","oval.s2","grammar","In “She traced an oval,” oval is used as ___.",["a noun naming a shape","an adverb of direction","a verb meaning to bake"],"a noun naming a shape","The article an and verb traced show oval is a count noun here.","grammar"),Q("oval.q3","oval.s1","context","Which object is most likely oval?",["an egg-shaped mirror","a square tile","a three-sided road sign"],"an egg-shaped mirror","An egg shape is the model for an oval form.","context"),Q("oval.q4","oval.s2","word-choice","The artist drew an ____ around the portrait.",["oval","ovary","ovation"],"oval","The blank names a rounded, elongated figure.","word-choice")]});
D("ovary",{etymology:E("From New Latin ovarium, formed from Latin ovum ‘egg’ + -arium, the place or receptacle suffix; the term names an egg-producing organ in animals and the seed-bearing part of a flower.",null,"Latin ovum","-arium","Etymonline, ovary (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ovary)."),contexts:[C("ovary.s1","生物","The scan showed a small cyst on one ovary, so the doctor scheduled a follow-up examination.","掃描顯示一側卵巢上有小囊腫，因此醫師安排了後續檢查。","Ovary is the female reproductive organ in which eggs are produced.","Count noun after one; so connects the scan finding with the next step.","The medical scan concerns a human reproductive organ."),C("ovary.s2","植物","After pollination, the flower’s ovary develops into fruit and contains the young seeds.","授粉後，花的子房發育成果實，並含有幼小種子。","In botany, an ovary is the part of a flower that contains young seeds.","Possessive flower’s identifies the plant structure; develops into gives the result.","Pollination and seed development select the botanical sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A flower’s ovary contains the petals but never holds young seeds.","A flower’s ovary contains the young seeds and can develop into fruit.","The botanical ovary contains ovules that develop into seeds; petals are separate flower parts.")],quiz:[Q("ovary.q1","ovary.s1","meaning","In human anatomy, an ovary is an organ where ___.",["eggs are produced","food is digested","air is filtered"],"eggs are produced","The animal sense is the female reproductive organ that produces eggs.","meaning"),Q("ovary.q2","ovary.s2","meaning","In a flower, the ovary contains ___.",["young seeds or ovules","the roots","the outer bark"],"young seeds or ovules","The botanical ovary holds the developing seeds and may form fruit.","meaning"),Q("ovary.q3","ovary.s2","context","Which change involves a flower’s ovary?",["It develops into fruit after pollination.","It becomes the plant’s root system.","It turns into a bird’s egg."],"It develops into fruit after pollination.","The ovary is the flower part that develops into fruit after fertilization.","context"),Q("ovary.q4","ovary.s1","word-choice","A scan of the reproductive organ found a cyst on the patient’s ____.",["ovary","oval","ovation"],"ovary","The medical context calls for the egg-producing organ.","word-choice")]});
D("ovation",{etymology:E("From Latin ovatio, the name of a Roman triumphal celebration of lesser rank than a triumph; modern English uses it for prolonged applause praising a performance or speech.",null,"Latin ovatio",null,"Etymonline, ovation (https://www.etymonline.com/word/ovation)."),contexts:[C("ovation.s1","艺术","The pianist received a loud ovation after the final movement, with the audience clapping for several minutes.","最後一個樂章結束後，鋼琴家獲得熱烈掌聲，觀眾鼓掌了好幾分鐘。","Ovation is sustained, enthusiastic applause praising a performance or speech.","Received an ovation is a collocation; after marks the performance’s end.","The audience’s prolonged applause shows strong public praise.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The speaker received an ovation, but the audience remained silent and left before the speech ended.","The speaker received an ovation as the audience applauded enthusiastically after the speech.","An ovation is sustained applause, not silence or an early departure.")],quiz:[Q("ovation.q1","ovation.s1","meaning","A performer who receives an ovation is given ___.",["prolonged enthusiastic applause","a private written warning","a medical examination"],"prolonged enthusiastic applause","Ovation names loud, sustained clapping in praise.","meaning"),Q("ovation.q2","ovation.s1","context","Which event would most likely end with an ovation?",["A moving concert performance","A silent equipment check","A routine bill payment"],"A moving concert performance","An audience may applaud enthusiastically to praise a performance.","context"),Q("ovation.q3","ovation.s1","collocation","The comedian’s final joke earned a standing ____. ",["ovation","ovary","outwash"],"ovation","Standing ovation is the established phrase for enthusiastic applause while standing.","collocation"),Q("ovation.q4","ovation.s1","meaning","What does an ovation communicate?",["strong public approval","an unpaid balance","a direction away from a center"],"strong public approval","The applause expresses praise for a speech or performance.","meaning")]});
D("oven",{etymology:E("Old English ofen, from Proto-Germanic *uhnaz and related Germanic forms; the noun names a heated chamber for cooking or industrial treatment.",null,"Proto-Germanic *uhnaz",null,"Etymonline, oven (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oven)."),contexts:[C("oven.s1","饮食","She baked the bread in the oven until the crust turned golden brown.","她把麵包放進烤箱烘烤，直到外皮變成金黃色。","A kitchen oven is an appliance used for baking or roasting food.","In the oven marks location; until introduces the baking result.","Bread and browning crust identify the household cooking appliance."),C("oven.s2","工业","The ceramics workshop fired the clay tiles in a large industrial oven.","陶藝工坊在大型工業窯爐中燒製黏土磚。","An oven can be a heated chamber for drying, firing, or hardening materials.","In a large industrial oven marks the heating chamber; fired is a technical verb.","Clay tiles are being fired in a heated chamber rather than cooked as food.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The baker roasted vegetables in a refrigerator oven that kept the food cold.","The baker roasted vegetables in a heated oven that cooked them thoroughly.","An oven heats food; a refrigerator keeps it cold, so the phrase is contradictory.")],quiz:[Q("oven.q1","oven.s1","meaning","A kitchen oven is mainly used to ___.",["bake or roast food","freeze vegetables","wash dishes"],"bake or roast food","The household appliance heats food for baking and roasting.","meaning"),Q("oven.q2","oven.s2","meaning","A ceramics oven is used to ___.",["fire or harden clay","keep a room dark","cool fresh bread"],"fire or harden clay","Industrial ovens heat materials such as clay tiles.","meaning"),Q("oven.q3","oven.s1","context","Where should a loaf bake?",["in a preheated oven","in a freezer","in a sink"],"in a preheated oven","Baking requires the heated chamber of an oven.","context"),Q("oven.q4","oven.s2","word-choice","The factory placed the tiles in a high-temperature ____ to harden them.",["oven","ovation","outskirt"],"oven","An industrial oven is a heated chamber used to fire or harden materials.","word-choice")]});
D("over",{etymology:E("From Old English ofer, from Proto-Germanic *uberi and an Indo-European form meaning ‘above or across’; its many senses include position, crossing, excess, completion, and repetition.",null,"Proto-Germanic *uberi",null,"Etymonline, over (https://www.etymonline.com/word/over)."),contexts:[C("over.s1","通用","A clean cloth lay over the bowl to keep dust out.","一塊乾淨的布蓋在碗上，以免灰塵落入。","Over means above or resting on top so as to cover something.","Preposition over introduces the covered object; to keep gives purpose.","The cloth lies on top of the bowl and covers its opening."),C("over.s2","通用","The cyclist rode over the bridge before the storm reached the valley.","暴風雨抵達山谷前，騎車人騎過了橋。","Over can mean from one side of something to the other.","Preposition over marks the route across the bridge; before gives timing.","The cyclist travels across the bridge from one side to the other."),C("over.s3","数量","The museum welcomed over 2,000 visitors during the festival.","節日期間，博物館接待了兩千多名訪客。","Over means more than a number or amount.","Over precedes the numeral 2,000; during sets the period.","The count exceeds 2,000 rather than equaling or falling below it."),C("over.s4","通用","The repair is over, so the residents can use the elevator again.","維修已經結束，因此居民可以再次使用電梯。","Over means finished or completed.","Predicate adjective after is; so introduces the consequence.","The elevator is usable again because the repair work has ended."),C("over.s5","口语","Turn the card over to read the instructions on its back.","把卡片翻過來，閱讀背面的說明。","Over can mean turn so another side is showing, or do something again.","Particle follows turn; to read states the purpose.","Turning the card makes its other side visible.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The card is over the table, meaning it is finished and no longer above it.","The card is over the table, meaning it is positioned above it.","In the spatial sense, over means above or covering; it does not mean finished here.")],quiz:[Q("over.q1","over.s1","meaning","A blanket over a child is ___.",["covering the child from above","more than one child","finished"],"covering the child from above","This sense describes something positioned above or covering another thing.","meaning"),Q("over.q2","over.s2","context","Which route goes over the river?",["A footbridge crosses from one bank to the other.","A path stops before reaching the river.","A boat stays tied to one bank."],"A footbridge crosses from one bank to the other.","Over can describe movement across an obstacle from one side to another.","context"),Q("over.q3","over.s3","meaning","Over 50 pages means ___.",["more than 50 pages","exactly 50 pages only","fewer than 50 pages"],"more than 50 pages","Before a number, over means greater than.","meaning"),Q("over.q4","over.s4","meaning","If the meeting is over, it is ___.",["finished","about to begin","taking place above the room"],"finished","Over can mean completed or ended.","meaning")]});
