D("overabundance",{etymology:E("Formed from over- ‘too much’ + abundance, from Latin abundantia ‘plenty’; it means more of something than is useful or wanted.","over-","abundance",null,"Etymonline, over- (https://www.etymonline.com/word/over-); Merriam-Webster, abundance (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/abundance)."),contexts:[C("overabundance.s1","通用","An overabundance of ripe tomatoes forced the market to lower its prices.","成熟番茄供應過多，迫使市場降價。","Overabundance means more of something than is useful or wanted.","An overabundance of + noun; forced introduces the consequence.","The surplus is large enough to push prices down.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The overabundance of clean water meant the town had almost none to drink.","The overabundance of clean water meant the town had far more than it needed.","Overabundance means an excessive amount, not a shortage.")],quiz:[Q("overabundance.q1","overabundance.s1","meaning","An overabundance of apples means there are ___.",["more apples than are needed","no apples available","exactly one apple"],"more apples than are needed","Overabundance is an excessive amount of something.","meaning"),Q("overabundance.q2","overabundance.s1","context","Which situation shows an overabundance?",["A warehouse is full of unsold winter coats after a mild season.","A shop has no coats left during a cold snap.","A tailor has one coat order."],"A warehouse is full of unsold winter coats after a mild season.","The supply exceeds what customers want.","context"),Q("overabundance.q3","overabundance.s1","collocation","A sudden ____ of applications slowed the review process.",["overabundance","outskirts","overcoat"],"overabundance","The noun fits an excessive quantity of applications.","collocation"),Q("overabundance.q4","overabundance.s1","meaning","Does overabundance usually describe too little or too much?",["Too much","Too little","Neither; only an exact amount"],"Too much","The prefix over- marks an excess beyond what is needed.","meaning")]});
D("overact",{etymology:E("A compound of over- ‘excessively’ and act; the verb means perform with too much dramatic emphasis on stage or screen.","over-","act",null,"Merriam-Webster, overact (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/overact)."),contexts:[C("overact.s1","文化","The director asked the actor not to overact the farewell scene, which needed quiet grief rather than shouting.","導演請演員不要把告別場面演得太誇張；這一幕需要安靜的悲傷，而不是大喊大叫。","Overact means perform too dramatically.","Not to + verb; the relative clause explains the desired restraint.","Shouting would make the emotional performance excessive for the scene.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The actor overacted the quiet scene by keeping every gesture subtle and restrained.","The actor performed the quiet scene subtly and did not overact it.","Overact means exaggerate a performance; subtle restraint is the opposite.")],quiz:[Q("overact.q1","overact.s1","meaning","An actor who overacts a scene ___.",["uses exaggerated emotion or gestures","forgets the lines completely","stands outside the theater"],"uses exaggerated emotion or gestures","Overact means perform too dramatically.","meaning"),Q("overact.q2","overact.s1","context","Which direction would prevent overacting?",["Show the sadness with a restrained voice.","Shout every line and wave both arms.","Turn every pause into a long speech."],"Show the sadness with a restrained voice.","A restrained delivery avoids excessive theatrical emotion.","context"),Q("overact.q3","overact.s1","grammar","Choose the infinitive: “The director told him not to ____.”",["overact","overacted","overacting"],"overact","Not to is followed by the base form of the verb.","grammar"),Q("overact.q4","overact.s1","word-choice","The performer exaggerated every reaction and began to ____.",["overact","overawe","overcast"],"overact","The verb names excessive dramatic performance.","word-choice")]});
D("overall",{etymology:E("The adjective and adverb combine over + all, first conveying ‘taking everything together’; the noun for work clothing is an independent plural-form use of overall garment.",null,"over + all",null,"Etymonline, overall (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overall)."),contexts:[C("overall.s1","通用","The overall design is simple, although each room has a different color scheme.","整體設計很簡潔，雖然每個房間的配色都不同。","Overall as an adjective means including all parts of a situation.","Attributive adjective before design; although marks a contrast.","The judgment considers the entire design, not an individual room."),C("overall.s2","通用","Overall, the repairs took less time than the estimate predicted.","總的來說，維修所花的時間比預估短。","Overall as an adverb means when everything is considered together.","Sentence adverb at the beginning summarizes the whole assessment.","It introduces a conclusion after considering all repair work."),C("overall.s3","生活","The painter wore blue overalls to keep splashes off his clothes.","油漆工穿著藍色工裝褲，避免衣服沾上濺出的油漆。","Overalls are loose work clothes worn over ordinary clothes.","Plural count noun as the object of wore; to keep gives purpose.","The garment protects the clothes underneath while painting.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","Overall, the workers wore an overview to protect their clothes from paint.","Overall, the workers wore overalls to protect their clothes from paint.","Overalls is the garment noun; overview means a general summary.")],quiz:[Q("overall.q1","overall.s1","meaning","The overall effect of a film considers ___.",["all its parts together","only its opening scene","the price of one ticket"],"all its parts together","Overall as an adjective concerns the whole situation.","meaning"),Q("overall.q2","overall.s2","context","Which sentence uses overall as a sentence adverb?",["Overall, the team met most of its goals.","The overall score was 86.","He put on his overalls."],"Overall, the team met most of its goals.","At the beginning it summarizes the assessment as a whole.","context"),Q("overall.q3","overall.s3","meaning","A mechanic’s overalls are ___.",["protective work clothes worn over other clothes","a summary of the repair","a long winter overcoat"],"protective work clothes worn over other clothes","This noun sense is work clothing that protects ordinary clothes.","meaning"),Q("overall.q4","overall.s3","grammar","Choose the plural garment noun: “The painters wore ____.”",["overalls","overall","overally"],"overalls","The work garment is normally referred to as plural overalls.","grammar")]});
D("overawe",{etymology:E("A compound of over- and awe; the verb means impress or frighten someone so strongly that they obey or feel unable to act freely.","over-","awe",null,"Merriam-Webster, overawe (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/overawe)."),contexts:[C("overawe.s1","心理","The young delegates were overawed by the general’s medals and formal manner, and agreed without asking questions.","年輕代表被將軍的勳章和正式態度震懾，沒有提問便同意了。","Overawe means frighten or impress someone so much that they obey.","Passive were + past participle; by introduces the cause.","Their compliance without questioning shows they were intimidated or deeply impressed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The visitors were overawed by the guide, so they freely ignored every instruction and did as they pleased.","The visitors were overawed by the guide and followed the instructions without protest.","Overawe means impress or intimidate enough to influence or control someone.")],quiz:[Q("overawe.q1","overawe.s1","meaning","A powerful official may overawe a witness by ___.",["intimidating the witness into silence","offering a friendly greeting","asking the witness to choose lunch"],"intimidating the witness into silence","Overawe means impress or frighten someone so strongly that they obey.","meaning"),Q("overawe.q2","overawe.s1","context","Which detail suggests the panel was overawed?",["They agreed immediately because the chair’s authority frightened them.","They calmly challenged the chair with evidence.","They left before meeting the chair."],"They agreed immediately because the chair’s authority frightened them.","Fearful compliance is the result of being overawed.","context"),Q("overawe.q3","overawe.s1","verb-form","Choose the past form: “The imposing building ____ the visitors.”",["overawed","overawe","overawing"],"overawed","The regular past form adds -d to overawe.","verb-form"),Q("overawe.q4","overawe.s1","word-choice","The ruler’s threats were intended to ____ the council into obedience.",["overawe","overbalance","overcoat"],"overawe","The verb means intimidate or impress people into compliance.","word-choice")]});
D("overbalance",{etymology:E("From over- + balance; as a verb it means tip or make something tip over, and as a noun it can name excess weight or value on one side.","over-","balance",null,"Merriam-Webster, overbalance (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/overbalance)."),contexts:[C("overbalance.s1","通用","The climber overbalanced while reaching for the upper hold and fell onto the safety mat.","攀岩者伸手去抓上方岩點時失去平衡，摔到了安全墊上。","Overbalance means tip over or make someone or something tip over.","Past-tense intransitive verb; while introduces the simultaneous action.","Reaching shifts the climber’s weight so far that balance is lost."),C("overbalance.s2","经济","The account showed an overbalance of costs on the first side of the ledger.","帳目顯示分類帳第一側的成本超出。","As a noun, overbalance can mean an excess of weight or value on one side.","An overbalance is the object of showed; of specifies the excess.","Costs exceed the values on the opposing side of the ledger.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","She overbalanced the ladder by keeping every load evenly distributed on both sides.","She kept the ladder balanced by distributing the load evenly on both sides.","Overbalance means lose or cause a loss of balance, not maintain an even balance.")],quiz:[Q("overbalance.q1","overbalance.s1","meaning","If a person overbalances on a ladder, they ___.",["tip past a stable position","remain perfectly steady","finish painting the wall"],"tip past a stable position","The verb sense is to tip over or lose balance.","meaning"),Q("overbalance.q2","overbalance.s2","meaning","An overbalance in a ledger indicates ___.",["an excess on one side","equal values on both sides","a missing page"],"an excess on one side","This noun sense is a surplus of weight or value on one side.","meaning"),Q("overbalance.q3","overbalance.s1","context","Which action shows overbalancing?",["A loaded cart tips when its weight shifts too far to one side.","A cart remains level on a flat floor.","A worker checks the cart’s label."],"A loaded cart tips when its weight shifts too far to one side.","The uneven load makes the cart tip over.","context"),Q("overbalance.q4","overbalance.s1","word-choice","He leaned too far and began to ____ toward the railing.",["overbalance","overawe","overcoat"],"overbalance","The verb describes losing balance and tipping.","word-choice")]});
D("overbearing",{etymology:E("A compound of over- + bearing, from bear ‘carry or exert’; the adjective describes someone who forces their will on others and expects obedience.","over-","bear","-ing","Etymonline, overbearing (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overbearing)."),contexts:[C("overbearing.s1","通用","The overbearing supervisor rejected every suggestion and insisted that the team follow her orders exactly.","專橫的主管否決了每個建議，堅持團隊完全服從她的命令。","Overbearing means domineering and forceful toward other people.","Attributive adjective before supervisor; and coordinates the behavior.","Rejecting all suggestions and demanding obedience shows domination.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The overbearing chair invited equal debate and accepted every member’s decision without pressure.","The considerate chair invited equal debate and accepted every member’s decision without pressure.","Those respectful actions contradict overbearing, which describes forcing one’s will on others.")],quiz:[Q("overbearing.q1","overbearing.s1","meaning","An overbearing manager tends to ___.",["force decisions on staff","invite open discussion","avoid giving any direction"],"force decisions on staff","Overbearing means domineering and expecting obedience.","meaning"),Q("overbearing.q2","overbearing.s1","context","Which behavior is overbearing?",["A supervisor interrupts everyone and demands unquestioned agreement.","A supervisor asks each person for input.","A supervisor shares the decision-making process."],"A supervisor interrupts everyone and demands unquestioned agreement.","The supervisor forces others to submit to their will.","context"),Q("overbearing.q3","overbearing.s1","word-formation","Choose the adjective: “The ____ landlord ignored every tenant’s concern.”",["overbearing","overbear","overbearingly"],"overbearing","The blank modifies landlord, so the adjective is needed.","word-formation"),Q("overbearing.q4","overbearing.s1","meaning","Which is the best contrast to an overbearing style?",["respectful and non-dominating","controlling and forceful","demanding obedience"],"respectful and non-dominating","A respectful style does not impose a person’s will on others.","meaning")]});
D("overburden",{etymology:E("Formed from over- ‘too much’ + burden; the verb means load a person, system, or structure with more than it can bear.","over-","burden",null,"Etymonline, overburden (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overburden)."),contexts:[C("overburden.s1","工作","The new reporting rule may overburden small clinics that already lack administrative staff.","新的報告規定可能使本來就缺乏行政人員的小診所負荷過重。","Overburden means place more demands on a person or system than it can handle.","May + verb; clinics is the object; that clause describes their existing constraint.","The clinics have little staff, so added reporting demands exceed capacity.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The extra cases overburdened the team, leaving everyone with less work than before.","The extra cases overburdened the team, leaving everyone with more work than before.","Overburden means impose too much load; the consequence should be excessive work, not less.")],quiz:[Q("overburden.q1","overburden.s1","meaning","To overburden a support team is to ___.",["give it more work than it can handle","reduce its workload to zero","move it to another building"],"give it more work than it can handle","Overburden means load beyond capacity.","meaning"),Q("overburden.q2","overburden.s1","context","Which change might overburden a small clinic?",["Adding many forms without adding staff","Removing unnecessary paperwork","Hiring enough clerks to manage the workload"],"Adding many forms without adding staff","The extra administrative work may exceed the clinic’s capacity.","context"),Q("overburden.q3","overburden.s1","grammar","Complete: “The sudden demand could ____ the network.”",["overburden","overburdened","overburdening"],"overburden","Could is followed by the base form.","grammar"),Q("overburden.q4","overburden.s1","word-choice","Too many assignments may ____ the students before exams.",["overburden","overawe","overcast"],"overburden","The verb describes imposing more work than they can comfortably manage.","word-choice")]});
D("overcast",{etymology:E("Formed from over- + cast, literally ‘cast over’; as an adjective it describes a sky completely covered by cloud.","over-","cast",null,"Etymonline, overcast (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overcast)."),contexts:[C("overcast.s1","气象","The overcast sky hid the sun throughout the afternoon, and the temperature stayed cool.","整個下午陰雲遮住了太陽，氣溫也一直偏涼。","Overcast describes a sky completely covered with cloud.","Attributive adjective before sky; and links two weather effects.","The sun is hidden by widespread cloud cover.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The forecast called for an overcast sky, with no clouds and bright sunshine all day.","The forecast called for a clear sky, with no clouds and bright sunshine all day.","Overcast means cloud-covered; a cloudless sunny sky is clear instead.")],quiz:[Q("overcast.q1","overcast.s1","meaning","An overcast afternoon is usually ___.",["cloudy with the sun hidden","cloudless and blazing","filled with falling snow only"],"cloudy with the sun hidden","Overcast describes a sky covered by cloud.","meaning"),Q("overcast.q2","overcast.s1","context","Which forecast predicts overcast weather?",["Cloud will cover the sky through the day.","The sky will remain cloudless.","Only a brief shower will pass beneath clear skies."],"Cloud will cover the sky through the day.","Complete cloud cover is the defining condition.","context"),Q("overcast.q3","overcast.s1","word-choice","The hikers packed a lamp because the ____ sky made the trail dim.",["overcast","overcoat","overawe"],"overcast","A cloudy sky can block sunlight and make the trail dim.","word-choice"),Q("overcast.q4","overcast.s1","meaning","What is hidden on an overcast day?",["the sun behind cloud cover","the road beneath water","a bill in an envelope"],"the sun behind cloud cover","Overcast indicates widespread clouds obscuring the sun.","meaning")]});
D("overcharge",{etymology:E("A compound of over- ‘too much’ + charge; the verb means ask someone to pay more than is fair or than the proper price.","over-","charge",null,"Etymonline, overcharge (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overcharge)."),contexts:[C("overcharge.s1","商务","The repair shop overcharged us for a replacement part that costs half as much elsewhere.","這家修理店對替換零件收費過高；別處的價格只有一半。","Overcharge means ask someone to pay too much money.","Past-tense verb with us as object; for introduces the item.","The price is far above the cost elsewhere, so the customer was charged too much.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The shop overcharged the customer by billing the exact advertised price and no extra fees.","The shop charged the customer the advertised price and did not overcharge them.","Charging exactly the stated price without extra fees is not charging too much.")],quiz:[Q("overcharge.q1","overcharge.s1","meaning","A hotel that overcharges a guest asks the guest to pay ___.",["too much","the agreed amount","nothing at all"],"too much","Overcharge means ask for more money than is fair or correct.","meaning"),Q("overcharge.q2","overcharge.s1","context","Which receipt suggests an overcharge?",["A $20 item is billed as $45 without explanation.","The listed $20 price is charged exactly.","A coupon reduces the price."],"A $20 item is billed as $45 without explanation.","The customer is asked to pay more than the stated price.","context"),Q("overcharge.q3","overcharge.s1","grammar","Choose the past tense: “The vendor ____ us for delivery.”",["overcharged","overcharge","overcharging"],"overcharged","The completed past action takes the -ed form overcharged.","grammar"),Q("overcharge.q4","overcharge.s1","word-choice","The mechanic added an unfair fee and tried to ____ the customer.",["overcharge","overcast","overawe"],"overcharge","The verb names asking a customer to pay too much.","word-choice")]});
D("overcoat",{etymology:E("Formed from over + coat; the garment is a long outer coat worn over ordinary clothes, especially in cold weather.",null,"over + coat",null,"Etymonline, overcoat (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overcoat)."),contexts:[C("overcoat.s1","衣着","He hung his wool overcoat by the door after walking home through the snow.","他冒雪走回家後，把羊毛大衣掛在門邊。","An overcoat is a long coat worn over ordinary clothes.","Count noun as the object of hung; after marks the completed walk.","The garment is worn over other clothing for warmth."),C("overcoat.s2","生活","Her heavy overcoat kept the wind from reaching the layers beneath it.","她厚實的御寒外衣擋住了寒風，保護裡面的衣層。","Overcoat can refer to the outer winter garment that protects against cold.","Possessive her modifies the garment; from introduces what it blocks.","The clothing functions as an outer layer against cold wind.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","He put his overcoat under his shirt as the innermost layer against the cold.","He put his overcoat over his clothes as the outermost layer against the cold.","An overcoat is worn over ordinary clothes, not as the innermost layer.")],quiz:[Q("overcoat.q1","overcoat.s1","meaning","An overcoat is normally worn ___.",["over ordinary clothes","under a shirt","as a pair of shoes"],"over ordinary clothes","The coat is an outer garment, often used in cold weather.","meaning"),Q("overcoat.q2","overcoat.s2","context","Which situation calls for an overcoat?",["Walking outside in freezing wind","Taking a shower","Swimming in a warm pool"],"Walking outside in freezing wind","The winter outer garment protects the wearer from cold.","context"),Q("overcoat.q3","overcoat.s1","word-choice","She buttoned her long ____ before leaving in the snow.",["overcoat","overbalance","overawe"],"overcoat","The sentence names the long outer coat worn in cold weather.","word-choice"),Q("overcoat.q4","overcoat.s2","meaning","What does an overcoat protect from?",["cold and wind","a bank overdraft","cloud cover"],"cold and wind","Its function is to insulate the wearer from cold weather.","meaning")]});
D("overcome",{etymology:E("From Old English ofer-cuman ‘come over, prevail’; the compound developed senses of successfully controlling a problem and being affected so strongly one cannot act normally.",null,"Old English ofer + cuman",null,"Etymonline, overcome (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overcome)."),contexts:[C("overcome.s1","通用","With steady practice, Nia overcame her fear of speaking in front of the class.","透過持續練習，妮婭克服了在全班面前發言的恐懼。","Overcome means succeed in controlling a problem, fear, or opponent.","Past-tense verb with fear as object; with introduces the means.","Practice lets her control and get past the fear."),C("overcome.s2","情感","He was overcome with grief when he heard that his closest friend had died.","得知摯友去世時，他悲痛得難以自持。","Be overcome with an emotion means be affected so strongly that normal action is difficult.","Passive be + overcome; with introduces the overwhelming emotion.","The grief is so intense that it overwhelms him.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","She was overcome of relief when the missing child returned.","She was overcome with relief when the missing child returned.","The standard phrase is be overcome with an emotion.")],quiz:[Q("overcome.q1","overcome.s1","meaning","To overcome a language barrier is to ___.",["succeed in dealing with it","make it impossible to communicate","pretend it does not exist"],"succeed in dealing with it","This sense means successfully control or defeat a problem.","meaning"),Q("overcome.q2","overcome.s2","meaning","If someone is overcome with laughter, they ___.",["are affected so strongly they struggle to act normally","are quietly bored","have defeated a rival"],"are affected so strongly they struggle to act normally","The passive phrase means an emotion overwhelms the person.","meaning"),Q("overcome.q3","overcome.s2","collocation","Complete: “She was overcome ____ emotion.”",["with","by to","at"],"with","The standard collocation is overcome with an emotion.","collocation"),Q("overcome.q4","overcome.s1","context","Which sentence uses overcome to mean defeat a difficulty?",["The crew overcame the shortage by sharing supplies.","He was overcome with sleepiness.","She felt overcome by laughter."],"The crew overcame the shortage by sharing supplies.","They successfully deal with the supply problem.","context")]});
D("overconfidence",{etymology:E("A compound of over- ‘excessively’ + confidence, from Latin confidentia; it means confidence greater than the facts justify.","over-","confidence",null,"Etymonline, over- (https://www.etymonline.com/word/over-); Merriam-Webster, confidence (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/confidence)."),contexts:[C("overconfidence.s1","心理","Overconfidence led the driver to enter the flooded road despite the warning signs.","過度自信使駕駛人無視警告標誌，駛入淹水道路。","Overconfidence is a level of confidence greater than the evidence supports.","Uncountable noun as subject; led + object + to-infinitive gives consequence.","The driver’s certainty exceeds the safety evidence and leads to a reckless choice.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Her overconfidence was fully justified because she checked every fact and recognized every risk.","Her confidence was justified because she checked every fact and recognized every risk.","Overconfidence is excessive certainty beyond what facts justify; careful risk assessment does not by itself show excess.")],quiz:[Q("overconfidence.q1","overconfidence.s1","meaning","Overconfidence can cause a person to ___.",["underestimate risks because they trust their ability too much","check every risk carefully","avoid making any judgment"],"underestimate risks because they trust their ability too much","Overconfidence exceeds what evidence warrants and can reduce caution.","meaning"),Q("overconfidence.q2","overconfidence.s1","context","Which decision suggests overconfidence?",["A novice skips safety checks because he assumes nothing can go wrong.","A pilot follows the checklist before takeoff.","A student asks for help with an unfamiliar tool."],"A novice skips safety checks because he assumes nothing can go wrong.","His certainty is greater than his experience and evidence support.","context"),Q("overconfidence.q3","overconfidence.s1","word-formation","The noun for excessive certainty is ____. ",["overconfidence","overconfident","confidently"],"overconfidence","The blank after is needs the abstract noun overconfidence.","word-formation"),Q("overconfidence.q4","overconfidence.s1","meaning","What distinguishes overconfidence from justified confidence?",["It goes beyond what the facts support.","It always follows careful evidence review.","It means having no belief in one’s ability."],"It goes beyond what the facts support.","The defining feature is confidence exceeding the evidence.","meaning")]});
D("overconfident",{etymology:E("Formed from over- + confident, from Latin confidentem ‘trusting’; it describes being too certain of one’s ability and neglecting caution.","over-","confident",null,"Etymonline, over- (https://www.etymonline.com/word/over-); Etymonline, confident (https://www.etymonline.com/word/confident)."),contexts:[C("overconfident.s1","通用","The overconfident climber skipped the weather check and started up the exposed ridge.","過度自信的攀登者跳過天氣檢查，便開始攀登暴露的山脊。","Overconfident means too certain of one’s ability, so care is neglected.","Attributive adjective before climber; and coordinates the risky actions.","Skipping a safety check reflects unjustified certainty and reduced caution.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The overconfident driver checked the mirrors repeatedly because he doubted his ability to park.","The cautious driver checked the mirrors repeatedly because he doubted his ability to park.","Overconfident describes excessive certainty, whereas doubt and careful checking indicate caution.")],quiz:[Q("overconfident.q1","overconfident.s1","meaning","An overconfident student may ___.",["assume they need no preparation","carefully review weak topics","ask a teacher to check their work"],"assume they need no preparation","Too much confidence can lead someone to neglect necessary care.","meaning"),Q("overconfident.q2","overconfident.s1","context","Which driver seems overconfident?",["One who speeds because he assumes his skill makes the road harmless","One who slows down in heavy rain","One who checks the route before leaving"],"One who speeds because he assumes his skill makes the road harmless","The driver trusts ability beyond what the conditions justify.","context"),Q("overconfident.q3","overconfident.s1","grammar","Choose the adjective: “The ____ bidder ignored the cost estimate.”",["overconfident","overconfidence","overconfidently"],"overconfident","The blank modifies bidder and therefore needs an adjective.","grammar"),Q("overconfident.q4","overconfident.s1","meaning","Why can being overconfident be risky?",["A person may neglect precautions.","A person always notices every danger.","A person never makes a decision."],"A person may neglect precautions.","Excessive certainty can make someone careless about risks.","meaning")]});
D("overcrowd",{etymology:E("A compound of over- ‘too much’ and crowd; the verb means put more people or things into a space than it can comfortably hold.","over-","crowd",null,"Etymonline, over- (https://www.etymonline.com/word/over-); Merriam-Webster, overcrowd (https://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/overcrowd)."),contexts:[C("overcrowd.s1","通用","The organizers reduced ticket sales so they would not overcrowd the small hall.","主辦方減少售票，以免小禮堂過於擁擠。","Overcrowd means put too many people or things into a space.","So that clause gives purpose; overcrowd takes hall as object.","Limiting tickets prevents occupancy from exceeding the room’s capacity.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The venue was overcrowded, with only ten people in a hall designed for a thousand.","The venue was nearly empty, with only ten people in a hall designed for a thousand.","Overcrowded means filled with too many people or things, not sparsely occupied.")],quiz:[Q("overcrowd.q1","overcrowd.s1","meaning","To overcrowd a bus is to ___.",["put more passengers on it than it can comfortably hold","remove every passenger","repair its engine"],"put more passengers on it than it can comfortably hold","The verb means fill a space with too many people or things.","meaning"),Q("overcrowd.q2","overcrowd.s1","context","Which action avoids overcrowding a room?",["Limit attendance to the room’s safe capacity.","Sell unlimited tickets for a tiny room.","Close the only exit."],"Limit attendance to the room’s safe capacity.","Capacity limits prevent too many people entering.","context"),Q("overcrowd.q3","overcrowd.s1","grammar","Complete: “Too many chairs could ____ the corridor.”",["overcrowd","overcrowded","overcrowding"],"overcrowd","Could takes the base form of the verb.","grammar"),Q("overcrowd.q4","overcrowd.s1","word-choice","The school moved the assembly outdoors to avoid ____ the gym.",["overcrowding","overcoat","overawe"],"overcrowding","The gerund names the condition of putting too many people into the gym.","word-choice")]});
D("overdo",{etymology:E("From over- + do; the verb means take an action too far, exaggerate, or cook something longer than needed.","over-","do",null,"Etymonline, overdo (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overdo)."),contexts:[C("overdo.s1","通用","You can add more lemon later, so do not overdo the seasoning at the start.","之後還可以再加檸檬，所以一開始不要把調味加得太重。","Overdo means carry an action or amount too far.","Do not + base verb; at the start specifies when.","Too much seasoning can overwhelm the dish, so restraint is needed.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The cook overdid the vegetables by steaming them for one minute until they stayed crisp.","The cook barely cooked the vegetables by steaming them for one minute until they stayed crisp.","Overdo means take something too far, such as cooking it too long; brief cooking that leaves it crisp is not overdoing it.")],quiz:[Q("overdo.q1","overdo.s1","meaning","If you overdo an apology, you ___.",["make it excessive","forget to apologize","write it in another language"],"make it excessive","Overdo means carry an action too far or exaggerate it.","meaning"),Q("overdo.q2","overdo.s1","context","Which cooking choice overdoes the vegetables?",["Boil them until they are mushy and flavorless","Steam them briefly until crisp","Serve them raw in a salad"],"Boil them until they are mushy and flavorless","Cooking them too long takes the action beyond what is needed.","context"),Q("overdo.q3","overdo.s1","verb-form","Choose the correct past form: “I ____ the praise and embarrassed her.”",["overdid","overdoed","overdoing"],"overdid","Overdo is irregular; its past tense is overdid.","verb-form"),Q("overdo.q4","overdo.s1","word-choice","The designer added so many decorations that she began to ____ it.",["overdo","overdraft","overawe"],"overdo","The context describes taking decoration too far.","word-choice")]});
D("overdraft",{etymology:E("From over- + draft, from the banking sense of drawing money; an overdraft is the amount withdrawals exceed an account balance when the bank permits it.","over-","draft",null,"Etymonline, overdraft (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overdraft)."),contexts:[C("overdraft.s1","金融","The bank charged interest on the overdraft after the account balance fell below zero.","帳戶餘額降到零以下後，銀行對透支金額收取利息。","Overdraft is the amount by which withdrawals exceed the account’s available money.","On the overdraft identifies what accrued interest; after gives the trigger.","The negative balance represents more money withdrawn than the account held.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","Her account had an overdraft because it contained more money than she could spend.","Her account had an overdraft because withdrawals exceeded its available balance.","An overdraft occurs when withdrawals exceed funds in the account, not when there is a surplus.")],quiz:[Q("overdraft.q1","overdraft.s1","meaning","A bank overdraft occurs when ___.",["withdrawals exceed the money in the account","a deposit raises the balance","the account is closed with a zero balance"],"withdrawals exceed the money in the account","An overdraft is the excess of withdrawals over available funds.","meaning"),Q("overdraft.q2","overdraft.s1","context","Which account has an overdraft?",["It has $40 available but a $65 payment is allowed.","It has $65 available and a $40 payment clears.","It has no transactions and a positive balance."],"It has $40 available but a $65 payment is allowed.","The allowed payment exceeds available funds by $25.","context"),Q("overdraft.q3","overdraft.s1","word-choice","The bank notified him that his ____ was $120 below zero.",["overdraft","overcoat","overcast"],"overdraft","The banking term names the amount drawn beyond the account balance.","word-choice"),Q("overdraft.q4","overdraft.s1","meaning","A fee on an overdraft is connected with ___.",["spending beyond the available account balance","wearing a coat in winter","a cloudy sky"],"spending beyond the available account balance","The financial term concerns withdrawals exceeding funds.","meaning")]});
D("overdue",{etymology:E("A compound of over- + due; it describes something not paid, returned, or arrived by its set time, and can mean a needed event should already have happened.","over-","due",null,"Etymonline, overdue (https://www.etymonline.com/word/overdue)."),contexts:[C("overdue.s1","通用","The library emailed a reminder because two borrowed books were overdue.","圖書館寄來提醒，因為借出的兩本書已逾期未還。","Overdue means not returned or completed by the time set.","Predicate adjective after were; because explains the reminder.","The due date has passed and the books remain unreturned."),C("overdue.s2","评价","After years of unequal pay, many employees felt that a salary review was long overdue.","多年薪資不平等之後，許多員工覺得薪資檢討早就該進行了。","Overdue can mean something should have happened already because it has been needed for a long time.","Long overdue is a predicate phrase; that clause gives the reason.","The delay has lasted so long that the review is now needed urgently.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The overdue library book was returned two weeks before its due date.","The overdue library book was returned two weeks after its due date.","Overdue means the due date has passed, not that an item was returned early.")],quiz:[Q("overdue.q1","overdue.s1","meaning","An overdue bill has ___.",["passed its payment deadline","been paid before it was issued","no due date"],"passed its payment deadline","This sense is not paid or settled by the stated time.","meaning"),Q("overdue.q2","overdue.s2","meaning","A reform described as long overdue is ___.",["needed for a long time and should already have happened","too early to consider","already canceled"],"needed for a long time and should already have happened","The evaluative sense expresses that a needed change has been delayed.","meaning"),Q("overdue.q3","overdue.s1","context","Which item is overdue?",["A library book still out after its return date","A book returned a day early","A book borrowed today"],"A library book still out after its return date","The scheduled return date has passed.","context"),Q("overdue.q4","overdue.s2","word-choice","After years of warnings, the safety upgrade is ____.",["long overdue","overdraft","overcast"],"long overdue","The upgrade should have happened already because it has been needed for a long time.","word-choice")]});
D("overestimate",{etymology:E("Formed from over- ‘too much’ + estimate, from Latin aestimare ‘value’; as a verb it judge too high, and as a noun an estimate that is too high.","over-","estimate",null,"Etymonline, estimate (https://www.etymonline.com/word/estimate)."),contexts:[C("overestimate.s1","通用","We overestimated the walking time and reached the cabin before sunset.","我們高估了步行時間，因此在日落前就到達小屋。","Overestimate as a verb means think an amount or ability is greater than it is.","Past-tense verb with walking time as object; and links the consequence.","The journey took less time than the estimate predicted."),C("overestimate.s2","通用","The first cost estimate was an overestimate, since the final bill was much lower.","最初的費用估算偏高，因為最後帳單低得多。","Overestimate as a noun is a judgment or figure that is too high.","An overestimate is a predicate noun; since gives evidence.","The final amount falls well below the initial figure.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The contractor called the low forecast an overestimate because it was far below the final cost.","The contractor called the high forecast an overestimate because it was far above the final cost.","An overestimate is too high; a figure below the actual amount is an underestimate.")],quiz:[Q("overestimate.q1","overestimate.s1","meaning","To overestimate a risk is to judge it ___.",["greater than it really is","smaller than it really is","impossible to measure"],"greater than it really is","The verb means assess an amount or risk too highly.","meaning"),Q("overestimate.q2","overestimate.s2","meaning","A project’s overestimate is ___.",["a figure that is too high","a figure that is too low","the exact final cost"],"a figure that is too high","This noun sense names an excessive estimate.","meaning"),Q("overestimate.q3","overestimate.s1","context","Which sentence uses overestimate as a verb?",["They overestimated the crowd and ordered too many seats.","The initial figure was an overestimate.","Their estimate was copied into the report."],"They overestimated the crowd and ordered too many seats.","Overestimated is an action of judging the crowd size too high.","context"),Q("overestimate.q4","overestimate.s2","grammar","Choose the noun: “The original cost was an ____.”",["overestimate","overestimated","overestimating"],"overestimate","After an, the sentence needs the noun for a figure that is too high.","grammar")]});
D("overexploit",{etymology:E("A compound of over- ‘excessively’ and exploit, from French exploiter; the verb means use a natural resource or workforce so heavily that the source is damaged.","over-","exploit",null,"Etymonline, exploit (https://www.etymonline.com/word/exploit)."),contexts:[C("overexploit.s1","环境","Fishing fleets overexploited the bay until local cod stocks could no longer recover.","漁船過度捕撈海灣，直到當地鱈魚資源無法恢復。","Overexploit means take so much from a resource that its source is damaged.","Past-tense transitive verb with bay as object; until marks the consequence.","The fish stock cannot recover because extraction exceeded a sustainable level.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The community overexploited the forest by harvesting only fallen branches and allowing every tree to regrow.","The community managed the forest sustainably by taking only fallen branches and allowing trees to regrow.","Overexploit means use a resource beyond a sustainable level; careful limited harvesting is not overexploitation.")],quiz:[Q("overexploit.q1","overexploit.s1","meaning","To overexploit a fishery is to ___.",["take fish faster than the stock can recover","protect the fish population from capture","count fish without catching them"],"take fish faster than the stock can recover","Overexploitation damages the resource by exceeding sustainable use.","meaning"),Q("overexploit.q2","overexploit.s1","context","Which practice may overexploit a forest?",["Cutting trees faster than they can regrow","Replanting after selective harvest","Protecting young trees from damage"],"Cutting trees faster than they can regrow","The extraction rate exceeds the forest’s ability to recover.","context"),Q("overexploit.q3","overexploit.s1","verb-form","Choose the past tense: “The company ____ the groundwater.”",["overexploited","overexploit","overexploiting"],"overexploited","The completed past action uses overexploited.","verb-form"),Q("overexploit.q4","overexploit.s1","word-choice","The fleet continued to ____ the stock despite declining fish numbers.",["overexploit","overcoat","overcast"],"overexploit","The verb describes extracting too much from a natural resource.","word-choice")]});
D("overexploitation",{etymology:E("Formed from over- + exploitation, itself from exploit; it names use of a natural stock or workforce beyond a sustainable or fair level.","over-","exploitation",null,"Etymonline, exploit (https://www.etymonline.com/word/exploit)."),contexts:[C("overexploitation.s1","环境","Overexploitation of the reef fish has reduced catches for every village along the coast.","珊瑚礁魚類遭到過度捕撈，沿岸各村的漁獲量都因此下降。","Overexploitation is use of a resource beyond a sustainable or fair level.","Of the reef fish identifies the resource; has reduced gives the consequence.","Declining catches show the fish stock is being depleted faster than it can recover.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report called the harvest overexploitation even though it stayed below the stock’s natural replacement rate.","The report called the harvest sustainable because it stayed below the stock’s natural replacement rate.","Overexploitation means use beyond a sustainable level; staying below replacement is sustainable use.")],quiz:[Q("overexploitation.q1","overexploitation.s1","meaning","Overexploitation of a forest occurs when ___.",["use exceeds the forest’s ability to recover","trees are planted faster than they are cut","the forest is left untouched"],"use exceeds the forest’s ability to recover","The noun describes extraction beyond a sustainable level.","meaning"),Q("overexploitation.q2","overexploitation.s1","context","Which report describes overexploitation?",["A fish population falls because catches remain above its recovery rate.","A fish population stays stable under limited catches.","A reef is protected from fishing."],"A fish population falls because catches remain above its recovery rate.","The resource is taken faster than it can replenish.","context"),Q("overexploitation.q3","overexploitation.s1","word-formation","The noun for exploiting a resource too much is ____. ",["overexploitation","overexploit","overexploited"],"overexploitation","The abstract noun names the excessive process.","word-formation"),Q("overexploitation.q4","overexploitation.s1","meaning","What is a likely result of overexploitation?",["a depleted resource","automatic renewal of the resource","a guaranteed increase in supply"],"a depleted resource","Taking more than can be replaced reduces the available stock.","meaning")]});
